From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:03:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: enable UFS

Enable the UFS host and its PHY. VCC is the fixed always-on regulator
cheetah and lynx use: stock drives it from gpp0-1 (boot-on), and the
bootloader leaves it on.

omamobile.ufs-probe tells the omarchy-mobile initramfs to load the UFS
drivers and apply its storage guard, which leaves only slot B's boot
images and userdata writable.

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B: four LUNs and 55 partitions enumerate,
with the same names and numbers as stock's by-name map, and the guard
leaves sda20-24 (slot B's boot images) and sda31 (userdata) read-write.
The Arch root on userdata boots from it.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts  | 29 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index 936a87241..c57880a45 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -2,9 +2,9 @@
 /*
  * Google Pixel 7 (panther) - first-light board file.
  *
- * USB (NCM + ACM), the cluster watchdogs from gs201.dtsi and a
- * simple-framebuffer on the buffer ABL leaves DPP0 scanning out. The panel
- * driver, touch, the GPU and UFS stay disabled.
+ * USB (NCM + ACM), the cluster watchdogs from gs201.dtsi, a
+ * simple-framebuffer on the buffer ABL leaves DPP0 scanning out, and UFS.
+ * The panel driver, touch and the GPU stay disabled.
  */
 
 /dts-v1/;
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ / {
 
 	chosen {
 		/* ABL requires bootargs to exist; it appends its own after these. */
-		bootargs = "console=tty0 panic=10 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused rdinit=/init";
+		bootargs = "console=tty0 panic=10 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused rdinit=/init omamobile.ufs-probe";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges;
@@ -45,6 +45,18 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer@fac00000 {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * UFS VCC. Stock drives it from GPIO gpp0-1 (boot-on), as on
+	 * cheetah; there is no gs201 GPIO driver yet, so describe it as
+	 * always on, as the bootloader leaves it.
+	 */
+	ufs_0_fixed_vcc_reg: regulator-ufs-vcc {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "ufs-vcc";
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+
 	reserved-memory {
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
@@ -76,3 +88,12 @@ &usbdrd31_phy {
 &usb_dwc3 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&ufs_0 {
+	vcc-supply = <&ufs_0_fixed_vcc_reg>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ufs_0_phy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
